WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.120
What happened to the heroes&nbsp;
of the "Predator" movies?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:07.440
Why are Predators so attracted to heat?&nbsp;
What's the reasoning behind their methods?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:10.640
Watch for even more questions we&nbsp;
may never know the answers to.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:16.240
To date, no character — human or otherwise&nbsp;
— has been featured in more than one film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:19.520
in the Predator franchise. The&nbsp;
lack of any recurring characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:23.760
is one of the franchise’s strengths,&nbsp;
but it does leave one curious as to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:27.440
how each human moves on with their&nbsp;
life after surviving the Yautja.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.520
Each sequel has attempted to have&nbsp;
Schwarzenegger reprise his role&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:37.920
as Alan Dutch Schaefer, but he's refused, leaving&nbsp;
the character's fate hazy for decades. In 2020,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:43.280
Arnold gave in for the 2020 video game, Preda&nbsp;
tor: Hunting Grounds. This game includes audio&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:49.120
journals accounting for Dutch's actions&nbsp;
between 1987 and the game's 2025 setting.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:53.440
According to the journals, Dutch has been&nbsp;
traveling the world, searching for more evidence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:58.560
of the Yautja's presence on Earth. He teams&nbsp;
up with the Other Worldly Life Forms Program,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:04.320
the shady government agency from Predator 2. As&nbsp;
the Earth gets hotter, Predators visit frequently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:08.560
leading to repeated battles between&nbsp;
Dutch and the Yautja. By 2025,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:13.760
he's been rebuilt using Yautja tech,&nbsp;
fearless and fit, despite his advanced age.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:16.480
"This thing is hunting us....all of us"

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:22.480
Across the Predator franchise, the Yautja&nbsp;
have demonstrated a common modus operandi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:27.280
that includes a few signature kills. No&nbsp;
Predator film would be complete, for instance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:31.120
without someone having their skull and&nbsp;
spine ripped out of their bodies in one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:35.760
swift motion. The Yautja remove skulls&nbsp;
and spines to display them as trophies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:40.080
and add bones to their armor to show off&nbsp;
their killing prowess. Their reasoning behind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:44.640
flaying a victim and leaving their bodies&nbsp;
behind, however, is a little more murky.

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:48.960
The intention behind hanging their skinned&nbsp;
prey is still the subject of debate among&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:53.520
fans. The Yaujta do not appear to collect&nbsp;
the skins they remove from their victims,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:58.240
so it's clearly the bodies themselves that are&nbsp;
important to the ritual. It's likely that these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:02.720
bodies are left as a form of intimidation&nbsp;
to throw their next opponents off balance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:07.840
There's also a theory that only those considered&nbsp;
easy prey are flayed, as they are unworthy of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:12.560
having their bones collected as trophies. "Not&nbsp;
only did I kill this guy," this action says,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:16.320
according to this theory, "but I even&nbsp;
had time to rip his skin off afterwards.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:19.840
If you don't want the same thing to happen&nbsp;
to you, you'd better be more entertaining."

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:25.920
In Predator, rebel Anna tells the mercenaries that&nbsp;
their stalker matches the description of, quote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:31.040
"the demon who makes trophies of man," from&nbsp;
local folklore. The stalkers are said to only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:35.120
appear during the hottest summers. When&nbsp;
the Yautja return to Earth in Predator 2,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:37.920
it's during a record-breaking heat wave in LA.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:41.680
Predator: Hunting Grounds implies that&nbsp;
climate change has made the Earth a more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:45.200
attractive place to hunt. The natural&nbsp;
assumption to make is that the heat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:49.040
mirrors that of the Yautja's natural&nbsp;
habitat, and that a hot summer is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:53.200
time during which the Earth is most&nbsp;
habitable for both humans and Yautja.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:59.200
As the series progresses, the Yautja's preference&nbsp;
in climate is less emphasized. Alien vs. Predator&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:04.960
reveals some Yautja visit every 100 years — in&nbsp;
Antarctica. Furthermore, Aliens vs. Predator:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:10.640
Requiem is set in Colorado, and the story is&nbsp;
explicitly set near Halloween in The Predator.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:15.360
This doesn't mean that the Predators don't still&nbsp;
prefer the heat, but it does remove its necessity.

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:21.760
In Predator 2, Mike Harrigan discovers an&nbsp;
alien hunter, nicknamed "City Hunter" by fans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:26.720
has been on an undercover killing spree. The&nbsp;
film concludes with Harrigan chasing the Predator&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:31.520
to his ship and killing him. However, other&nbsp;
Yautja have been watching all of this unfold,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:36.320
hidden by cloaking technology. They retrieve&nbsp;
the dead Predator's body and leave LA.

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:41.120
Out of this group of Yautja, only one is seen&nbsp;
making kills. It's unclear if the others simply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:45.840
haven't been caught, remain on the ship the entire&nbsp;
time, or if they are here on other business.&nbsp;

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:50.800
Only one member of the Los Angeles hunting party —&nbsp;
their leader, Greyback — ever appears again in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:55.680
Predator expanded universe, and that story does&nbsp;
not account for his whereabouts during Predator 2.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:04:03.360
" You can't see the eyes of the&nbsp;
demon, until him come calling."

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:08.000
At the end of Predator 2 Harrigan receives a&nbsp;
trophy from the Yautja leader for killing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:13.600
City Hunter. It's a flintlock pistol&nbsp;
labeled "Raphael Adolini, 1715."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:17.440
This gift is evidence that the Yautja&nbsp;
have been hunting on Earth for centuries.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:24.640
The 1996 comic Predator: 1718 depicts the original&nbsp;
encounter between the Yautja known as Greyback and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:30.240
pirate captain Raphael Adolini. Andolini,&nbsp;
a criminal with a righteous moral compass,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:34.640
wants to return a chest of gold to the church&nbsp;
from which it was stolen. His crew objects and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:40.080
mutinies. Greyback surprisingly joins Adolini&nbsp;
and together they defeat his traitorous crew.

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:43.840
Andolini is lethally injured and offers&nbsp;
Greyback his pistol as a tribute.

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:50.320
The protagonist of Alien vs. Predator is Lex&nbsp;
Woods, an expert ice climber hired to guide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:56.080
an expedition to explore an ancient temple beneath&nbsp;
an Antarctic island. Lex survives being picked off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.080 --> 00:05:02.000
by the xenomorphs and Yautja, and allies herself&nbsp;
with the Yautja hunter Scar. She receives a Yautja&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:07.440
Combistick weapon as a trophy, and much of her&nbsp;
fate after the Yautja craft departs is unknown.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:12.720
Lex's arc hasn't been revisited or referenced&nbsp;
in any expanded universe material. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:16.160
there is a piece of evidence that&nbsp;
Lex, or at least her weapons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:20.560
were recovered from the Antarctic&nbsp;
battle site. In 2018's The Predator,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:26.480
Dr. Casey Brackett explores Project Stargazer's&nbsp;
headquarters and finds a case containing Lex's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:31.520
spear. This seems to confirm that Alien vs.&nbsp;
Predator is still part of the Predator canon.

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:36.960
The action of Alien vs. Predator takes place&nbsp;
inside an ancient temple in Antarctica,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:40.960
the site of a ritual where adolescent&nbsp;
Yautja prove themselves against the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:46.160
universe's ultimate killing machines. Inside&nbsp;
the temple lies an enslaved xenomorph queen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:50.400
kept in hibernation for a century at&nbsp;
a time. A few hours before a hunt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:55.120
she's forced to lay eggs so that the Yautja&nbsp;
will have something to test themselves against.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:06:00.400
In 2004's ritual, the queen gets wise and&nbsp;
instructs her children to set her free by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:05.520
melting her chains with their acidic blood. At&nbsp;
the film's climax, the queen escapes the temple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:10.960
into the abandoned town, and battles on the ice&nbsp;
with Lex and Scar, the last human and Yautja.&nbsp;

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:15.360
They successfully chain her to a heavy iron&nbsp;
vat and push it into the freezing water.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:19.520
The queen drops to the bottom of the sea&nbsp;
and is presumably no longer a threat.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:24.240
Other films in the Alien series have shown that&nbsp;
xenomorphs are capable of enduring the freezing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:29.360
airless vacuum of space. It is likely the queen&nbsp;
could survive these conditions for a while or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:34.640
even forever! Nevertheless, the Antarctic queen&nbsp;
has never reappeared in the franchise's canon.

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:40.000
Aliens vs. Predator: Requiem picks&nbsp;
up where the first AvP leaves off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:45.440
with a xenomorph chestburster emerging from&nbsp;
Scar's corpse. This xenomorph has taken on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:50.000
many of the traits of its Yautja host&nbsp;
to become the even deadlier "Predalien".&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:55.040
When the Predalien crash-lands a spacecraft&nbsp;
loaded with xenomorph eggs in Colorado,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:59.440
another Predator, Wolf, is set loose to&nbsp;
clean up the mess. Wolf battles with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:03.840
Predalien and a hoard of xenomorphs, but&nbsp;
this battle is moot — the story ends with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:09.280
the US government dropping a nuke on the village,&nbsp;
destroying almost all evidence of the conflict.

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:14.960
In the final scene, US Army Colonel Stevens&nbsp;
presents Ms. Yutani with a plasma pistol&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:18.640
fashioned by Wolf. Yutani seems to&nbsp;
have plans for the pistol that are,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:23.760
quote, "not for this world." It's implied that&nbsp;
Yutani plans to reverse-engineer the technology&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:27.600
to advance her company's interests in&nbsp;
space, leading to the Weyland-Yutani&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:33.120
Corporation's dominance of space freight and&nbsp;
xenomorph experimentation in the Alien series.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:38.000
Requiem doesn't have a sequel so we don't have&nbsp;
many details on what will happen next. Also,&nbsp;

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:44.000
the release of Prometheus in 2012 detached the&nbsp;
Alien franchise from the continuity of AvP,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:46.880
leaving the future of the&nbsp;
Yutani Corporation uncertain.

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:53.360
2010's Predators takes the action off Earth&nbsp;
entirely, and follows a group of humans who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:58.400
are each abducted and transported to a planet&nbsp;
that is a massive game preserve. Each of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:03.200
human captives is a predator in their own&nbsp;
right — a soldier, a convict, a gangster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:07.440
and so on — but most of them are no match for&nbsp;
their pursuers, who are bigger and badder than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:13.120
any Yautja seen previously. They're picked off&nbsp;
one by one until the only survivors are American&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:19.200
mercenary Royce and IDF sniper Isabelle. Predators&nbsp;
ends with Isabelle and Royce victorious over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:24.320
their hunters, but still stranded on the planet,&nbsp;
where another hunting season is about to begin.

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:28.560
Unlike most protagonists in the Predator&nbsp;
franchise, Isabelle and Royce received a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:33.920
follow-up story immediately, in the form of&nbsp;
an official sequel comic: 2010's Predators:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:37.840
Preserve the Game. The one-shot comic&nbsp;
picks up two months after the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:42.000
as Royce and Isabelle continue to pick&nbsp;
off Predators and salvage their gear.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:46.800
The Yautja determine Royce is a worthy opponent,&nbsp;
and gifts him his own set of Predator armor to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:51.920
wear in one-on-one battle against a four-armed&nbsp;
super-Yautja. But Royce learns to depend on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:56.720
someone else for a change and sets himself&nbsp;
up as bait so that Isabelle can get the kill.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.720 --> 00:09:00.960
They remain trapped on the planet, waiting&nbsp;
for an opportunity to hijack a starship.

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:07.280
In The Predator, another Yautja comes to Earth.&nbsp;
But this time, he's not here to hunt — he's on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:12.960
run from the larger, genetically-enhanced Upgrade&nbsp;
Predator. The Fugitive crash-lands in Mexico,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:17.360
but not before ejecting a pod containing&nbsp;
some precious cargo. By the end of the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:21.760
both Predators are dead. With the help&nbsp;
of young linguistic genius Rory McKenna,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:26.720
US military scientists are able to determine&nbsp;
that the rebel Predator came to Earth to deliver&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:32.000
the humans a weapon: A powered suit of armor&nbsp;
called the Predator-Killer. Rory's father,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:36.880
Army Ranger Quinn McKenna, plans to wear it&nbsp;
in battle next time the Yautja come calling.

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:41.520
But why did the Fugitive Predator decide to&nbsp;
give this weapon to humanity in the first place?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:46.160
Does it have anything to do with the human DNA&nbsp;
found in his blood? If he's here to help us,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:51.040
he's got a funny way of showing it, as he kills&nbsp;
nearly every person he sees during his time on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:56.320
our planet. His apparently benevolent intentions&nbsp;
are only revealed in the final scene of the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:59.360
a teaser for a sequel that has never happened.

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:03.760
This last-minute twist may be the result of&nbsp;
the film's reshoots, which reportedly changed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:08.640
a great deal of the film's overall plot. In&nbsp;
fact, in one of the three filmed endings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:13.600
the Fugitive's cargo pod contains Ellen&nbsp;
Ripley, heroine of the Alien films.

